<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/20th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · War</p><h1 class="enc-title">Falklands War</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1982</span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Falklands War was a ten-week conflict in 1982 between <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/argentina">Argentina</a> and the United Kingdom over the Falkland Islands and South <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/georgia">Georgia</a>. Argentina's military junta occupied the islands on 2 April, and a British task force retook them, forcing an Argentine surrender at Stanley on 14 June. About 650 Argentine and 255 British servicemen died, and the defeat hastened the fall of Argentina's dictatorship.</p></div>
